Original Swift 4.2.4 Ubuntu 18.04 SDK fixture, x86_64-linux only.

This recipe preserves the original Swift compiler and SwiftPM implementations.
The compiler reports 4.2.4; the bundled SwiftPM reports Swift 4.2.0. These are
distinct upstream release strings and must remain unchanged.

Packaging adjusts ELF loader metadata and ordinary C runtime search paths using
the same verified wrapper as the Swift 5.5.3 fixture. The original glibc module
map's 79 absolute header paths are relocated to real Nix headers. Every module
directive remains present, and reversing those path substitutions must restore
the original bytes. The recipe records each header hash and the reverse check.
The archived Ubuntu libedit ABI-2 payload is copied intact; no ABI-name aliases
stand in for a different implementation.

The source-owned build hook uses the native option surface and product metadata:
it omits the unsupported parallel-job option and reads product_type. It does not
rewrite manifest language versions or synthesize SDK API answers. No editor
server is supplied by this fixture.

The recipe is test infrastructure, not an exhaustive runtime support claim.
Portable dependency-state format 2 and pure build behavior require their own
actual native consumer checks. Local development keeps the installed runtime;
it does not install this fixture automatically.
